About the Role
As Xiaohongshu (RED) scales internationally, our risk & safety systems, platforms and data infrastructure need to land and run independently overseas. We are looking for a versatile engineer in the US to own the local adaptation, integration and stability of our risk systems, serving as the Owner of the region's risk engineering. As a single-person regional post, we expect you to both build/adapt and independently own operations and stability.
Responsibilities
Local Development
: Take over the mature risk engine, platform and data infrastructure from China; handle local adaptation, integration and necessary secondary development to run independently in the US;
Iteration & Integration
: Follow HQ capability upgrades — integrate, test and iterate locally; handle region-specific business and technical needs;
Stability Ownership (baseline requirement)
: As regional Owner, independently safeguard system stability — monitoring/alerting, troubleshooting, rate-limiting, degradation, failover and incident response; be first to step up and resolve issues yourself;
Data Compliance
: Ensure local systems comply with US data privacy requirements (e.g. CCPA);
HQ Collaboration
: Stay aligned and version-synced with the China HQ risk team; collaborate across time zones in English and Mandarin.
Requirements
Bachelor's or above in CS-related fields; 3+ years backend development; strong engineering and coding fundamentals;
Able to fully own a system
— both develop/adapt/iterate and independently handle on-call and production issues (this is a hard baseline);
Familiar with high-concurrency systems and common stability practices (monitoring/alerting, rate-limiting, degradation, DR, observability);
Strong ownership, able to work independently; proficient in English and Mandarin for HQ collaboration;
Plus: background in risk control / trust & safety / content moderation, or cross-border landing/ops experience.
What You'll Gain
Own RED's US risk engineering end to end — from local development to stable operation;
A front-line international role bringing one of the industry's largest, most complex risk systems live and running independently overseas;
Deep collaboration with top engineering / algorithm / product teams at HQ, with compounding technical impact.

Responsibilities
Retargeting Pixels Setup
Implement and validate retargeting pixels, including page views, registrations, deposits, custom events, and user matching parameters;
Offer & Campaign Integration
Configure offers, tracking links, parameters, subIDs, macros, and campaign flows across tracking platforms and advertiser systems;
Technical Communication
Communicate with advertisers, affiliate networks, media buyers, and internal teams to clarify integration requirements and solve tracking issues;
Troubleshooting & Debugging
Investigate data mismatches, missing conversions, incorrect parameters, broken links, pixel errors, and attribution issues;
Documentation
Prepare clear integration instructions, checklists, and technical notes for each advertiser or campaign setup;
Postback Setup & Validation
Set up, test, and troubleshoot S2S postbacks for registrations, deposits, FTDs, revenue, and other key events.
Requirements
Experience with postback setup, offer tracking, and campaign integration - must have;
Experience with retargeting pixels, tracking events, GTM, browser pixels, or S2S tracking — must have;
Understanding of tracking parameters: click_id, sub_id, external_id, user_id, event_id, UTM tags;
Basic understanding of attribution models: post-click, post-view, deduplication;
Experience with tracking platforms, affiliate platforms, or ad networks.
Ability to test integrations using logs, preview links, browser dev tools, or tracking reports;
Understanding of media buying flows and conversion funnels;
Strong attention to detail and ability to quickly identify tracking issues;
English level sufficient for communication with partners.
